   "source": [
    "# 🧠 Self-Learning Wordle Agent\n",
    "\n",
    "**No LLM. No pre-programmed rules. Pure learning from experience.**\n",
    "\n",
    "The agent starts completely blind — it knows nothing about English words, letter frequencies, or strategy. It plays thousands of Wordle games and learns:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Which words are worth guessing (win-rate tracking per word)\n",
    "- Which letters are likely given feedback patterns (letter-position statistics)\n",
    "- How to prioritize candidates using what it's learned so far\n",
    "\n",
    "### Learning mechanism\n",
    "| Component | What it learns |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `word_scores` | Win rate when each word was used as guess 1 |\n",
    "| `letter_pos_freq` | How often each letter appears at each position in winning games |\n",
    "| `letter_freq` | Overall letter frequency from wins |\n",
    "| `pattern_memory` | Given a feedback pattern, which follow-up words worked |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Exploration vs. exploitation\n",
    "Early on the agent explores randomly. As it wins more games, it exploits learned knowledge — controlled by a decaying **epsilon** (ε) parameter.\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
